<title>MEXICO: Mexico to fix sorghum prices in Sinaloa next week.</title>
<headline>Mexico to fix sorghum prices in Sinaloa next week.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agriculture Ministry said on Tuesday it plans to fix sorghum prices in the northwestern state of Sinaloa next week.</p>
<p>In a statement, the ministry said the fixed prices will help to facilitate the sales of around 200,000 tonnes of sorghum expected to be grown in the state this cycle.</p>
<p>Throughout Mexico, farmers and the grains trade have been at loggerheads over domestic prices because of falling international grains prices.</p>
<p>In recent weeks, the government has stepped in and started to fix grains prices on a state-by-state basis to avoid prices wars between farmers and merchandisers, also offering subsidies.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
